{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Application - OAuth2 - Okta OAuth2 Client Secret Read",
	"Description": "Someone read an OAuth2 client's secret. Client secrets are written down once at setup; reading one later hands over API access as that client, so this should correspond to a known rotation.\n\nEvent type: app.oauth2.client.read_client_secret\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
